/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Two straights meet at the point of intersection I; the deflection angle Δ is the angle through which the forward straight turns from the back straight.
   - R in m, Δ in degrees.
   - Pegs go at full chainages (every 20 m or 30 m), with a sub-chord at each end.
   - Entering a circular curve straight from a tangent, a vehicle would meet the full radial acceleration V² ÷ R and superelevation at once.
   - V is the design speed in m/s, c the permitted rate of change of radial acceleration in m/s³ (about 0.3 to 0.6), R the radius in m, Ls the transition length in m.
   - Two gradients g₁ and g₂ (as decimals, + rising, − falling in the direction of chainage) meet at the vertical point of intersection.
   - r is the permitted rate of change of gradient per metre (sight distance may govern instead).
*/
